NAME
       truncate - shrink or grow a file to a given size

SYNOPSIS
       truncate [-c] -s SIZE FILE...

DESCRIPTION
       truncate sets the size of each FILE. Data past the new size is thrown
       away; when the file grows, the new part reads as zero bytes and takes
       no disk space (a sparse file). A missing FILE is created.

       truncate -s 0 empties a log file while a program still has it open,
       which deleting it would not do.

OPTIONS
       -s, --size=SIZE
              The new size, with units K, M, G (powers of 1024). +SIZE grows
              by that much, -SIZE shrinks by that much.

       -c, --no-create
              Do not create missing files.

EXAMPLES
           truncate -s 0 /var/log/myapp.log
           truncate -s 100M /root/test.img

SEE ALSO
       dd(1), fallocate(1), du(1)
